<Base title="about · poshitha">
  <h1 class="page-title"></h1>

  <div class="story">
    <p>
      i grew up in <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tirupati" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tirupati</a>,
      a small town in southern india known for being home to one of the
      <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venkateswara_Temple,_Tirumala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">largest temples</a>
      in the country. i come from a family of farmers and was raised in a
      traditional south indian family. as a
      first-generation college student, i have seen how deeply education can
      shape the direction of a person's life. my family has always been my
      backbone and has shaped much of how i see the world.
    </p>
    <p>
      for the final two years of high school, i moved across the country to
      attend <a href="https://www.jpischool.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">jayshree periwal international school</a>
      in jaipur. leaving home to live at a boarding school was one of the
      biggest turning points in my life. i met people whose lives looked
      completely different from mine, and the world suddenly felt much larger
      than the one i had known growing up.
    </p>
    <p>
      during high school, i started asking myself a question: what would i
      willingly stay up all night doing, even if nobody paid me? the answer i
      keep returning to is building technology alongside people who are equally
      excited to solve really hard problems.
    </p>
    <p>
      that journey eventually brought me to <a href="https://www2.lehigh.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lehigh</a>,
      where a full scholarship made it possible for me to study in the united
      states. here, i have tried to develop skills in the subjects i care about
      while doing one of my favorite things, bringing people together. that has
      led me to help lead the <a href="https://www.lehighsof.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">scholars of finance</a>
      chapter, become a resident assistant for first-year students, and build
      <a href="/projects">projects</a> with some incredibly curious people.
    </p>
    <p>
      beneath everything i do is a fairly simple north star: i want my work to
      help people. i do not know yet what form that will take. i want to work on
      difficult problems, create things, and eventually build something that can
      positively affect people at scale.
    </p>
    <p>
      i am still learning what i should spend my time doing and what kind of work is
      uniquely mine to do. for now, i am trying to follow my curiosity, learn
      through doing, stand behind what i believe, and not take life or myself
      too seriously along the way.
    </p>
    <p>
      please feel free to <a href="mailto:pou228@lehigh.edu">reach out</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ul class="trail">
    <li><a href="/food">food</a> <span class="muted">, places i'd send you, on a map</span></li>
    <li><a href="/movies">movies</a> <span class="muted">, the quest to watch a film from every country</span></li>
    <li><a href="/photos">photos</a> <span class="muted">, from everywhere i've been</span></li>
  </ul>

  <style>
    .story { max-width: 60ch; }
    .story p { margin: 0 0 18px; }
    .trail { list-style: none; margin: 40px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  </style>
</Base>
